# Smart-X API requests
# Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension, JetBrains Rider / IntelliJ HTTP client, or Visual Studio.
@api = http://localhost:5100

### Health
GET {{api}}/api/health

### Landing-page pillars
GET {{api}}/api/pillars

### Deployment locations (Facility › Zone › Sub-Zone)
GET {{api}}/api/topology/locations

### Register a new environmental sensor in Sub-Zone B
POST {{api}}/api/devices
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "macAddress": "24:0A:C4:BE:EF:01",
  "displayName": "B-09 Soil Moisture",
  "category": "Environmental",
  "subZoneId": "sz-b",
  "room": "Bed 9",
  "metric": "soil_moisture",
  "unit": "%",
  "expectedIntervalSeconds": 2,
  "minValue": 0,
  "maxValue": 100,
  "simulateTelemetry": false
}

### Registration REJECTED by recursive placement check (Zone 1 requires <= 10 s)
POST {{api}}/api/devices
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "macAddress": "24:0A:C4:BE:EF:02",
  "displayName": "B-10 Slow Sensor",
  "category": "Environmental",
  "subZoneId": "sz-b",
  "metric": "soil_moisture",
  "unit": "%",
  "expectedIntervalSeconds": 30,
  "minValue": 0,
  "maxValue": 100
}

### Push a float reading (TelemetryPacket<float>)
POST {{api}}/api/telemetry
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "deviceMac": "24:0A:C4:BE:EF:01",
  "payloadType": "float",
  "value": 41.7
}

### REJECTED: out of plausible range
POST {{api}}/api/telemetry
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "deviceMac": "24:0A:C4:BE:EF:01",
  "payloadType": "float",
  "value": 250
}

### REJECTED: wrong payload type for the device
POST {{api}}/api/telemetry
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "deviceMac": "24:0A:C4:BE:EF:01",
  "payloadType": "bool",
  "value": true
}

### Historical upload as a jagged array (batches of different lengths)
POST {{api}}/api/telemetry/batch
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "deviceMac": "24:0A:C4:BE:EF:01",
  "payloadType": "float",
  "intervalSeconds": 2,
  "batches": [
    [40.1, 40.3, 40.2],
    [40.6],
    [41.0, 41.2, 41.1, 40.9]
  ]
}

### Upload a hardware log (multipart)
POST {{api}}/api/devices/240AC4BEEF01/attachments
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=SmartXBoundary

--SmartXBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="kind"

HardwareLog
--SmartXBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="boot.log"
Content-Type: text/plain

[00:00:01] ESP32 boot OK
[00:00:02] Wi-Fi connected
--SmartXBoundary--

### Pulse Grid snapshot
GET {{api}}/api/pulse/snapshot

### Open incidents
GET {{api}}/api/incidents?openOnly=true

### Aggregate two meters (operator overloading)
GET {{api}}/api/meters/aggregate?ids=24:0A:C4:0C:00:10&ids=24:0A:C4:0C:00:11&tolerance=100

### Validate the live topology (recursion)
GET {{api}}/api/topology/validate

### Validate the deliberately broken sample
GET {{api}}/api/topology/samples/invalid

### Placement chain for a node
GET {{api}}/api/topology/nodes/sz-b/placement

### History matrix (multi-dimensional array)
GET {{api}}/api/zones/sz-a/history-matrix?slots=12

### Boxing vs generics evidence
GET {{api}}/api/diagnostics/boxing?count=200000

### Jagged batch demo
POST {{api}}/api/diagnostics/batch-demo?devices=50&batches=20&readings=120

### Simulate a gateway outage in Sub-Zone B
POST {{api}}/api/simulator/outage/sz-b?seconds=30

### Simulator status
GET {{api}}/api/simulator/status

###############################################################################
# PART 2: Real-Time Command Stream
###############################################################################

### Simulate a HIGH-PRIORITY alert: critical moisture drop (< 20 %) on a soil sensor.
# Replace the MAC with any Sub-Zone B soil sensor from GET {{api}}/api/stream/devices?query=b-01
POST {{api}}/api/telemetry
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "deviceMac": "24:0A:C4:0B:00:08",
  "payloadType": "float",
  "value": 12.5
}

### Same thing through the helper endpoint (picks a Sub-Zone B sensor for you)
POST {{api}}/api/alerts/simulate?kind=moisture

### Severe power spike (>= 4 kW) on a Sub-Zone C meter -> priority lane
POST {{api}}/api/alerts/simulate?kind=power

### Prove the bypass: 5,000 standard packets, then 1 critical packet
POST {{api}}/api/stream/burst?count=5000

### Queue statistics (both lanes)
GET {{api}}/api/stream/queue

### Pause / resume the dispatcher (watch the lanes fill up)
POST {{api}}/api/stream/queue/pause

###
POST {{api}}/api/stream/queue/resume

### Last processed packets (lane + wait time)
GET {{api}}/api/stream/recent?max=20

### O(1) lookup: exact MAC in any format
GET {{api}}/api/stream/devices?query=240ac40b0008

### Inverted-index search + filters (record=true teaches the engine)
GET {{api}}/api/stream/devices?query=pump%20a&record=true

###
GET {{api}}/api/stream/devices?category=Actuator

###
GET {{api}}/api/stream/devices?state=Offline

###
GET {{api}}/api/stream/devices?alertsOnly=true

### Timeline from the SortedDictionary
GET {{api}}/api/devices/240ac40b0008/timeline?minutes=15&maxPoints=120

### Dictionary vs List benchmark + hash collisions
GET {{api}}/api/diagnostics/lookup?devices=20000&lookups=5000

### Active alerts, disconnected HashSet, duplicates suppressed
GET {{api}}/api/alerts

### Device shadows (what devices poll)
GET {{api}}/api/commands/shadows

### Bulk override: close every valve in Sub-Zone C
POST {{api}}/api/commands
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "CloseAllValves",
  "subZoneId": "sz-c",
  "issuedBy": "rest-client"
}

### Undo the last command (Stack<T> pop)
POST {{api}}/api/commands/undo?issuedBy=rest-client

### Redo
POST {{api}}/api/commands/redo?issuedBy=rest-client

### Command history (undo + redo stacks)
GET {{api}}/api/commands/history

### Start the dry-out scenario for Sub-Zone B
POST {{api}}/api/simulator/dryout/sz-b

### Suggested actions + automated insights
GET {{api}}/api/engine

### What the engine has learned
GET {{api}}/api/engine/rules?top=15

### Global history (SortedDictionary), newest first
GET {{api}}/api/history?minutes=60
